        "repeat": "Inspected full2x2 repeats and actual1:1 Mid/High X/Y/four-corner grids. Original pale course network continues across edges, without an additional perimeter bevel or separate tile-border shading.",
        "relief": "Viewed actual source-bound mask overlay and both-tier decoded height/XYZ/opposed lights. Existing mortar network is lower than stone, while white deposits on faces remain on the upper surface; mask traces physical joints rather than brightness. Planar source-traced block boundaries are present in scalar height, but no additional visible contour defect is demonstrated in actual diffuse/opposed-light views. Independent three-mortar/six-face decoded patches plus three face-deposit samples support the classification. Scalar bands do not calibrate world displacement depth."
